  "_source": "Hand-verified directly against RCA-DFC-REG-002.md SS28 (0x3400-0x341C) per-field bit tables, cited by contract ID, and RCA-DFC-ARCH-002.md's dfc_rtl016_control_t/status_t Appendix B tables (OPEN_ISSUES.md item 90). SAFETY_CHANNEL_CONTROL/SAFETY_RESPONSE_MASK/SAFETY_INTERLOCK_MASK are each REG-002's own 'selected channel' register, declared in indexed_registers (reggen.py v5, same mechanism RTL-014/015's sessions built and reused, items 68/82) -- four real stores each, written/read at SAFETY_CHANNEL_SELECT.CHANNEL (REG-3408, REG-COH-001). The complete 4-channel bank is forwarded to dfc_rtl016_control_t's new safety_channel_c<0..3>__* fields (struct grown 53->226 bits this session: 172 bits for the 4-channel array, plus 1 bit for rtl016_evt_overflow_status__event_overflow, a real gap found while writing this field map -- Appendix B's first draft omitted RTL-016's own EVENT_OVERFLOW-clear-forwarding control field entirely, the 15th instance of this same gap class, item 6/item-82-precedent) since RTL-016 must evaluate PERMIT[c] for all four channels simultaneously and continuously -- a single selected-view field cannot carry that. Each of the three indexed registers' field list carries BOTH the struct's pre-existing selected-view fields (plain, driven by the indexed-register generator's own {name}_q selected-entry mux -- forwarded but functionally unused by dfc_rtl016.sv, item 73 precedent) AND the 4 new per-channel array entries, since every bit of the control struct must be covered by exactly one field-map entry and reggen.py keys control_registers by register name (one dict entry per register, not two). SAFETY_CONTROL/SAFETY_CHANNEL_SELECT are readback=internal_reg; SAFETY_STATUS/SAFETY_CHANNEL_STATUS/RTL016_EVT_OVERFLOW_STATUS are readback=external, closing the RTL-002/003/004-style host-READ gap (item 21) from the start.",
